      "node_id": "kg_doc_9",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Todtnauberg is a German village in Black Forest (\"Schwarzwald\") belonging to the municipality of Todtnau, in Baden-Württemberg. It is named after the homonym mount (\"berg\" means hill or mountain in German) and is famous because it is the place where the German philosopher Martin Heidegger had a chalet and wrote portions of his major work, \"Being and Time\".",
